    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Single-row inspection notes**\n",
        "\n",
        "This example shows how the dataset stores PII. The `source_text` column contains the original text. The `privacy_mask` column lists the PII categories and values found in the text. The `mbert_token_classes` column gives token-level labels, where `O` means not PII and labels like `B-EMAIL` or `I-EMAIL` mark PII tokens.\n",
        "\n",
        "For the main binary task, any row with a token label other than `O` should be labeled privacy-sensitive."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "F3xv2tOZ_Lnv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# make binary safe/pii label\n",
        "def is_sensitive(row):\n",
        "    tags = row.get('mbert_token_classes', None)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if tags is not None:\n",
        "        return int(any(str(t).strip() != 'O' for t in tags))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return 0\n",
        "\n",
        "# apply label function to every row\n",
        "df['label'] = df.apply(is_sensitive, axis=1)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NSa4XBOf-wrz"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": []
